{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it would be this:\n\nI'd give everyone the ability to truly *feel* what it's like to be someone else for a few minutes.\n\nNot just to hear another person's story, but to actually experience their life - their fears, their hopes, what keeps them up at night, what makes them feel loved.\n\nI think so much of the pain in the world - war, hate, loneliness, inequality, even just everyday meanness - comes from a failure of imagination. We forget that the stranger on the other side of the screen or the street is a full person, just as complex and real as we are.\n\nIf everyone had that kind of radical empathy, even briefly, I think a lot of other problems would start to fix themselves. You can't really ignore hunger, or injustice, or someone's loneliness when you've felt what it feels like to live it. People would be kinder not because they had to be, but because they'd *want* to be.\n\nThe practical part of me wants to say something more concrete like \"end scarcity of food, shelter, and education for every kid born anywhere\" - because that would also change everything. But I think the empathy comes first. Give people that, and they'll make sure everyone has what they need.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one change to make, what would you choose?",
